WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.101 --> 00:00:02.769
And then he slipped on it,
spit it out, and walked away.

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:04.170 align:start size:56% position:44%
That's disgusting.

00:00:04.203 --> 00:00:05.705 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Oh, hello. I'm Gav.
- I'm Dan.

00:00:05.738 --> 00:00:07.407 align:start position:0%
Welcome
to "The Super Slow Show."

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.075
Dan, I've noticed since we've
been out here in the desert

00:00:09.108 --> 00:00:11.144 align:start size:97% position:3%
- we're getting pretty tanned.
- Yeah.

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:12.745 align:start size:97% position:3%
- We're spending too much time
  under the sun.
- Absolutely true.

00:00:12.778 --> 00:00:15.782 align:start size:88% position:13%
Which is why I've built this
lovely break room for us.

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:18.151
- Lovely. Tremendous.
- You like the finish?

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:19.685 align:start position:0%
I love the finish.
You did a really
good job with it.

00:00:19.718 --> 00:00:21.320 align:start size:56% position:44%
Thanks.
I think the crew's
gonna be jealous.

00:00:21.353 --> 00:00:22.822 align:start position:0%
And we gotta kid it out
with, you know, home theaters

00:00:22.855 --> 00:00:24.657 align:start position:0%
and nice recliners,
couple of X-boxes...

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:27.393 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Yeah, yeah.
- lab coat steamers
  and probably a kettle.

00:00:27.426 --> 00:00:29.729 align:start size:91% position:9%
- Finish it off?
- I need to get my coffee
  that reminds me.

00:00:29.762 --> 00:00:31.731 align:start size:50% position:50%
You got the key?

00:00:31.764 --> 00:00:33.599 align:start position:0%
My key's inside.

00:00:33.632 --> 00:00:35.601 align:start position:0%
You didn't lock it.

00:00:35.634 --> 00:00:38.604 align:start position:0%
( sighs )

00:00:38.637 --> 00:00:39.806 align:start size:44% position:56%
You know what?

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:41.474 align:start size:59% position:41%
I put in--
remember I put that

00:00:41.507 --> 00:00:42.809 align:start size:44% position:56%
that extra way
in the house.

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:44.811 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Like the fail safe in case--
- Oh.

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:47.113 align:start position:0%
- The way to open the house
  in case we locked the keys in.
- Yeah, yeah

00:00:49.148 --> 00:00:50.316 align:start position:0%
What are the chances?

00:00:50.349 --> 00:00:52.218 align:start position:0%
Right when we move in
as well.

00:00:52.251 --> 00:00:54.654 line:0%
<i> ( music playing )</i>

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:03.463 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Have to get the locks
  changed again.
- I can't believe it.

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:05.098 align:start size:75% position:25%
- Yeah.
- How annoying.

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:07.100 align:start size:91% position:9%
- I never do that.
- I never do that either.

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:09.602 align:start size:63% position:38%
What happened to us?

00:01:09.635 --> 00:01:12.105 align:start size:75% position:25%
- Oh, well.
- ( Dan sighs )

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:23.583 align:start size:69% position:31%
Well, luckily I always
carry backups, eh?

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:26.219
Three, two, one!

00:01:27.486 --> 00:01:29.322
Dan:
Oh!

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:35.761 align:start position:0%
- ( distant car alarm blaring )
- May have--

00:01:35.794 --> 00:01:37.897 align:start size:97% position:3%
- May have overdone it there.
- I think you set off
  someone's car alarm.

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:39.298 align:start size:28% position:72%
That is--
Oh, yeah.

00:01:39.331 --> 00:01:40.567 size:78% position:39%
At least the door's open.

00:01:42.601 --> 00:01:44.704 size:75% position:38%
A bit excessive I think.

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:46.172 align:start size:69% position:31%
I mean it did the job,
though.

00:01:46.205 --> 00:01:47.607 align:start size:31% position:69%
It's true.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:49.142 align:start position:0%
You can't argue that it wasn't
a functional fail safe.

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:50.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Maybe I can get my coffee.
- Yeah.

00:01:50.409 --> 00:01:52.211 align:start position:0%
It's probably in there.

00:01:52.244 --> 00:01:54.814
You bought enough materials to
build another one, didn't you?

00:01:54.847 --> 00:01:56.516 align:start size:50% position:50%
Uh, that was it.

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:57.750
Ah.

00:01:57.783 --> 00:01:59.919 size:84% position:42%
Thankfully we recorded that

00:01:59.952 --> 00:02:03.222 align:start position:0%
at a thousand frames a second
and 2,000 frames a second
with two Phantom cameras.

00:02:03.255 --> 00:02:04.724 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Was handy--
- Was lucky I suppose.

00:02:04.757 --> 00:02:07.127 align:start position:0%
Let's go see
what it looked like.

00:02:09.528 --> 00:02:11.364 align:start size:91% position:9%
-<i> Oh! </i>
-<i> Look at the detonation.</i>

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:13.366
Dan:
<i> You see all the dust
 on the ground move.</i>

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:14.934
Gav:
<i> You see it already
 shook the camera.</i>

00:02:14.967 --> 00:02:18.771
<i> The shockwave just rushed
 towards the camera.</i>

00:02:21.874 --> 00:02:25.178
Dan:
<i>See how far some of that debris
 flung there?</i>

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:26.812 align:start size:72% position:28%
-<i> The debris. </i>
-<i> Debris.</i>

00:02:26.845 --> 00:02:29.415
Gav:<i> Some of the debris landed
 all the way back there.</i>

00:02:29.448 --> 00:02:32.452
<i> Must be about a hundred feet
 at least.</i>

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:38.891
<i> Oh, you see it blow out
 the windows before it goes.</i>

00:02:38.924 --> 00:02:40.760
Dan:
<i> Before anything happens
 the windows move.</i>

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:42.795
<i> That's so weird.</i>

00:02:50.836 --> 00:02:54.507
<i> The overpressure just causes
 the whole thing to burst.</i>

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:57.210
<i>It just-- the house just burst.
 It just popped essentially.</i>

00:02:57.243 --> 00:03:00.279
Gav:
<i> That would be incredibly
painful to be in front of that.</i>

00:03:00.312 --> 00:03:02.515
Dan:
<i> Well, yeah.
Your insides would be shook up.</i>

00:03:02.548 --> 00:03:03.716
Gav:
<i> What's interesting, though,</i>

00:03:03.749 --> 00:03:05.585
<i>is that this places around that</i>

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:07.320
<i> where if you stood you may
 not have been hit by anything.</i>

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:08.921
<i> Obviously you'd feel
 the pressure wave, but--</i>

00:03:08.954 --> 00:03:10.790
Dan:<i> That's a good point.
 I supposed if you were--</i>

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:13.593
<i> I reckon there's a spot at
 least like two meters away</i>

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:15.528 align:start size:97% position:3%
-<i> where you'd be absolutely-- </i>
-<i> And everything would just go
  to the side of you.</i>

00:03:15.561 --> 00:03:18.565 align:start size:88% position:13%
-<i> Yeah. </i>
-<i> You'd be such a badass
  if you stood there.</i>

00:03:25.337 --> 00:03:26.706
Gav:
<i> Explosions are always
 a lot more interesting</i>

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:29.575
<i> when it's very dusty out
 just because</i>

00:03:29.608 --> 00:03:31.978
<i> A, the shockwave lifts up a
 layer of dust in the ground</i>

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:33.613
<i>and it also sends stuff flying.</i>

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:35.648 align:start size:81% position:19%
-<i> More action. </i>
-<i> Much more action.</i>

00:04:00.973 --> 00:04:02.875 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Well, hopefully you--
- Oh, hang on.

00:04:02.908 --> 00:04:05.444
- ( Gav sighs )
- I'm sorry!

00:04:05.477 --> 00:04:06.779 align:start position:0%
Where was that?

00:04:06.812 --> 00:04:08.781 align:start size:78% position:22%
It was in the
inner pocket of a pocket.

00:04:08.814 --> 00:04:10.516 size:78% position:39%
